{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774364371,"nonce":"bAMTpc1ad+DdF9NfASKPd/CHZ2I=","title":"TPU multi-process parallelism: jax.distributed lockfile race condition on v4","message":"## Summary\n\nOn v4-8 TPU, attempting to run 3 independent training processes on separate chips fails due to libtpu lockfile race condition. Process 0 grabs /tmp/libtpu_lockfile during jax.distributed.initialize(), and processes 1 and 2 fail with \"Internal error when accessing libtpu multi-process lockfile.\"\n\nTPU_VISIBLE_CHIPS works for device visibility but doesn't help with the libtpu lock (only one process can hold it). jax.distributed.initialize() should coordinate the lock sharing but the race condition prevents this.\n\n## What we tried\n\n- TPU_VISIBLE_CHIPS=N per process: lock conflict\n- jax.distributed.initialize with coordinator_address/local_device_ids: lock race\n- Various launch timing (simultaneous, staggered): same result\n\n## Expected behavior\n\n3 processes, each with jax.distributed.initialize(local_device_ids=[i]), should coexist on a v4-8 TPU with each owning one chip.\n\n## Proposed solution\n\nInvestigate proper TPU multi-process setup. May need:\n- TPU_PROCESS_BOUNDS env var\n- Proper MEGASCALE_COORDINATOR setup\n- Or a different approach entirely (single process with pmap)\n\nThis would enable Feedbax Studio to parallelize training across TPU chips automatically.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e","files":null}]}